### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### RegionsController — /api/regions
### SEN PharmaFlow — compatible VS Code "REST Client" (Huachao)
### Fichier autonome : contient ses propres logins.
### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@password = Password123!
@regionThiesId = 10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000013


### 0a. Login — ADMIN_PNA
# @name loginAdminPna
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "cheikh.ba@sante.gouv.sn",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


### 0b. Login — GESTIONNAIRE_PNA
# @name loginGestionnairePna
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mamadou.diallo@sante.gouv.sn",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


### 0c. Login — ADMIN_PRA (pour le test de rôle insuffisant)
# @name loginAdminPra
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "abdoulaye.ndoye@sante.gouv.sn",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


### 1. POST /api/regions — créer une région (ADMIN_PNA / GESTIONNAIRE_PNA uniquement)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/regions
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdminPna.response.body.$.results.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "TEST-REG-{{$timestamp}}",
  "nom": "Région de test HTTP"
}


### 2. POST /api/regions — cas d'erreur, code déjà existant (409/422 attendu)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/regions
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdminPna.response.body.$.results.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "THIES",
  "nom": "Thiès (doublon)"
}


### 3. POST /api/regions — cas d'erreur, code invalide (caractères interdits, 400 attendu)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/regions
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdminPna.response.body.$.results.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "th!es",
  "nom": "Thiès"
}


### 4. POST /api/regions — cas d'erreur, champs manquants (400 attendu)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/regions
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdminPna.response.body.$.results.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "",
  "nom": ""
}


### 5. POST /api/regions — cas d'erreur, rôle insuffisant (403 attendu — ADMIN_PRA non autorisé)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/regions
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdminPra.response.body.$.results.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "TEST-FORBIDDEN",
  "nom": "Ne devrait pas être créée"
}


### 6. GET /api/regions — lister toutes les régions (les 14 régions + celles créées)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/regions
Authorization: Bearer {{loginGestionnairePna.response.body.$.results.accessToken}}


### 7. GET /api/regions/{id} — obtenir la région de Thiès
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/regions/{{regionThiesId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdminPna.response.body.$.results.accessToken}}


### 8. GET /api/regions/{id} — cas d'erreur, identifiant inexistant (404 attendu)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/regions/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdminPna.response.body.$.results.accessToken}}


### 9. GET /api/regions — cas d'erreur, sans authentification (401 attendu)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/regions
